.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt SHUTDOWN 2
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm shutdown
.Nd disable sends and receives on a socket
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/socket.h
.Ft int
.Fn shutdown "int s" "int how"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn shutdown
system call shuts down one or both directions of the socket
.Fa s ,
as
.Fa how
says:
.Bl -tag -width SHUT_RDWR
.It Dv SHUT_RD
Further receives return end-of-file.
On a local socket the data already queued, and any that arrives later, is
discarded, and descriptors sent with it are closed.
.It Dv SHUT_WR
Further sends fail with
.Er EPIPE .
The peer of a connection reads end-of-file once it has read what was sent;
a TCP connection sends its FIN.
.It Dv SHUT_RDWR
Both.
.El
.Pp
The socket stays open until its last descriptor is closed.
Once both directions are shut down,
.Xr poll 2
reports
.Dv POLLHUP .
.Pp
Local sockets of every type, and TCP connections, support
.Fn shutdown ;
a local stream or sequenced-packet socket must be connected.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBADF
.Fa s
is not an open descriptor.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa how
is not one of the values above.
.It Bq Er ENOTCONN
The local stream or sequenced-packet socket, or the TCP socket, is not
connected.
.It Bq Er ENOTSOCK
.Fa s
is not a socket.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The socket is a UDP or raw socket.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr close 2 ,
.Xr socket 2 ,
.Xr unix 4
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Fn shutdown
system call conforms to
.St -p1003.1-2008 .
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn shutdown
system call first appeared in
.Bx 4.2 .
